{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Until a month of days.</b> עד — and not inclusive of the end. That is, twenty-nine days, and they come to twenty days in Sivan, as stated in tractate Ta'anit." "<b>And it shall be to you לזרא.</b> The alef is in place of the letter heh, as in ״קראן לי מרא.״ And <b>לזרא</b> means to push away, as in ״נזורו אחור זרה הלאה״ — that is to say: you will eat from it meat, and its end will be evil and abhorrent to you, until you push it away and distance it from yourselves." "<b>לאמר.</b> 'Why did we come out of Egypt?' — and that which you said, ״We remember the fish״ etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:28.086779521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}